      "message": "Just making I understand: We only need to check the to-be-appended `src` against the \"expanded\" (old) `dst`, because the resulting copy will happen in-order? (eg, even if doing the expansion would cause `lastInstr`\u0027s src and dst to overlap, it\u0027s okay, because we\u0027ll always copy  sequentially, and read from the start of the new src before we overwrite it later in the op?",
